The region inside both A and B, 36, is the set {36}. This set is a subset of both A and B, and it represents the number of elements that are both perfect squares and whole numbers less than 50.

The region outside both A and B, the intersection of the complements of A and B, is the set {2, 6, 8, 10, 12, 15, 17, 18, 20, 22, 24, 26, 30, 33, 38, 40, 50}. This set represents the elements that are in either A or B, but not in both.

